 "preferred_name": "Endocannabinoid system",
 "kind": "knowledge",
 "definition": "The network of cannabinoid receptors and naturally made cannabinoid-like molecules in the body that helps regulate functions such as mood, appetite, pain and sleep.",
 "description": {
  "text": "A biological system made of endocannabinoids, which are neurotransmitters that bind to cannabinoid receptors, and the receptor proteins found throughout the central and peripheral nervous systems. It is found in animals as simple as hydras but is absent in insects.",
